---
description: Make frontend changes visible in the running application before handing them off
globs: web/**/*
alwaysApply: false
---

# Refresh the running frontend

- After changing frontend files, determine how the frontend is currently running.
- If the `auxilia-web` Docker container is running without a source bind mount, rebuild and recreate it with `docker compose up -d --build web`.
- If the Next.js development server is running, verify that hot reload picked up the change; restart it if needed.
- Wait for the frontend to become healthy and verify that it serves successfully before reporting completion.
- Do not assume that editing source files makes changes visible in a production Docker image.
